{
  "$comment": "DRAFT for approval. Not seeded. Tree of CMS category terms for Site Accelerator. Level 1 = the group a visitor sees in the Topic Hub (Category, Audience, Theme). Level 2 = the vertical (Banking, Insurance, Healthcare, Education, Retail, Technology, Public Sector), so each site can show only its own vertical. Leaves are what content gets tagged with. Names use letters, numbers and spaces only (the CMS key is the name with underscores). The same leaf name may repeat across verticals (Option A): the CMS prefixes the key, and the front end resolves keys through lib/taxonomy.ts, never by hand. Create parents before children, top to bottom. Content format (article, event...) is NOT a category: it comes from the content type.",
